			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">I have awakened in a city I do not recognise. And the people wear unfamiliar clothes. The city itself is larger then any I have ever seen before, and I fear I am lost. Where to go from here, I do not know. All I know is that I must find my friend, who I last saw in the city of Freeport.
<br />

<br />
_____________________________________________________________
<br />

<br />
   Before the cataclysms, I begged the gods to spare my life, and not to destroy the worlds. But to no success. Then, there was a bright flash in the sky. It was the moon; Luclin. what happened to it. 
<br />

<br />
   Yet as I turn my head to look upon the sky, the sky itself fell in the way of my view. Burning rocks were falling onto the lands around me....What could this be. But my mind was clouded with fear and worry. Before I knew it, one of the burning rocks from the sky, fell upon the ground, just next to me. When it landed, it exploded. Sending me flying several yards.
<br />

<br />
Then I began to feel dreary, as if I was tired. No longer could I hear the screams of my fellow man, nor feel the burns on my body. Nor longer could I even summon the strength to lift my arms, and pick myself up.
<br />

<br />
____________________________________________________________
<br />

<br />
   The next thing I knew, I was waking up in this body. One that I do not recognise as my own, with clothes that are not mine. When I realized, the gods did spare me. Just as I begged. I have been given another chance, and I must still be in the city of Qeynos. And this must be the new world of Norrath.
<br />

<br />
   I believe I was sent here by the Gods, not only to be spared. But help undo what was been done. Help save the people of this world from the cataclysms happening again, and repent for all our old sins.
<br />

<br />
   Perhaps others have been spared, and sent here as well. Those of us who can tell the stories of the old world. But who will believe us, Who will believe the world was ever how we once knew it. Or how we have travelled to this place.
<br />

<br />
   I suppose I will have to figure it out as I go. There is no time to waiste.</span><span class="gensmall"></span></td>
